# The image builds from source; a host `target/` would be both huge and useless
# (wrong platform, wrong toolchain) and would defeat the build cache mount.
target/

# Nothing in the image needs version control or editor state.
.git/
.gitignore
.idea/
.vscode/
.github/

# Not a workspace member: the Python demos talk to the engine over its socket and
# have no part in the Rust build.
python-demo/

# ...except the demo policy the socket all-in-one image bakes in, so that its
# `install` and `self-test` need no mounted files. A path re-included under an
# excluded directory has to come *after* the exclusion.
!python-demo/demo_policy.dw
!python-demo/demo_schema.cedarschema

# Local noise.
*.log
**/*.rs.bk
.DS_Store

# Note the deliberate omission: `Cargo.lock` is gitignored in this repository, so
# it is *not* excluded here. Copying the host's lock file is what lets the image
# build with `--locked` and get the same dependency graph the tests ran against.
